    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0339" n="323" xml:id="pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.24/6–1048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-10T17:00:00-04:00">June 10, 1948—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>372. Attention Marshall, Lovett and Armour.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d233-f1"/>
                    Report in press of recent sale to Argentina of a quantity of arms most
                    disturbing. In addition have been advised that Department of Army recently sold
                    fifty 90 mm guns which seems here to be preferential treatment for Argentina.
                    Effect here exceedingly bad and may hasten purchase from England of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ajax</hi> and other ships for the navy as well as all
                    types military equipment in open market by Chilean armed forces (Embtel 366,
                    June 9<anchor n="2" xml:id="d233-f2"/>). Unless Congress passes before
                    adjournment inter-American military cooperation act Chile probably will be
                    forced in self defense buy elsewhere than from US. Our prestige in military
                    circles was very high until recently but it has undergone slump which is most
                    disturbing to Embassy.</p>
                <p>It is impossible persuade Chileans to share in confidence of some quarters at
                    home in the peaceful intentions or the democracy of Perón. The fear of Argentine
                    intentions here is most real and in my opinion entirely justified. Suggest you
                    read military attaché’s report 89–48<anchor n="2" xml:id="d233-f3"/> to
                    Department of Army.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
